  - `model`: a definition/structure/class/instance of a model object (data, not a claim).
  - `statement-only`: statement present but proof admitted (body contains sorry / axiom / `by sorry`).
  - `upstream source claim`: the declaration is asserted upstream (e.g. blueprint/README/docs claim) without a Lean declaration we could verify; e.g. claims in docs, `\notready` blueprint nodes.

