For each declaration, compute:
- name, kind, line, module, file
- attributes present (preceding lines starting with @[)
- statement text: from declaration start to first top-level `:=` (depth-0) or `where`, or end of line for axioms/structures... For structure/class, statement = header up to `where`.
- body_sorry: whether a `sorry` token appears between this decl start and the next decl start (for top-level decls).
- admission: "admitted" if body contains sorry/admit or kind == axiom; else "clean".

