Build script `tools/d13_build_probes.sh`:
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# usage: d13_build_probes.sh [targets...]
set -u
WT=/data/.../D13-upstream-api-inventory-3602
export ELAN_HOME=$WT/.elan-home
export PATH=$ELAN_HOME/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.32.1/bin:$PATH  # or use elan
cd $WT/probes
mkdir -p $WT/logs
for t in "$@"; do
  log=$WT/logs/build-${t//./_}.log
  start=$(date +%s)
  lake build "$t" > "$log" 2>&1
  code=$?
  end=$(date +%s)
  echo "$t exit=$code seconds=$((end-start))" | tee -a $WT/logs/build-summary.txt
done
```
Note: `lake` from the elan bin dir uses ELAN_HOME to find the toolchain; since we installed the toolchain manually into $ELAN_HOME/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.32.1, elan should find it. Also need the toolchain to be "selected": since probes/lean-toolchain says leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1 and ELAN_HOME contains it, elan will use it. Good.

